---
import Prose from '../layouts/Prose.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Prose
  title="Terms and conditions"
  standfirst="The terms you buy under. Written to be read, not to be skipped."
  updated="TBD"
>
  <h2>Who you are buying from</h2>
  <dl>
    <dt>Trading name</dt>
    <dd><span class="tbd">{site.tradingName}</span></dd>
    <dt>Address</dt>
    <dd><span class="tbd">{site.tradingAddress}</span></dd>
    <dt>Email</dt>
    <dd><a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a></dd>
  </dl>
  <p>
    I am a sole trader based in the United Kingdom and not currently registered
    for VAT, so no VAT is charged on these prices.
  </p>

  <h2>Orders</h2>
  <p>
    Placing an order is an offer to buy. A contract forms when I email to
    confirm your order has been accepted. If I cannot fulfil it — a print
    failure, a colour I have run out of — I will tell you and refund you in
    full.
  </p>
  <p>
    Prices are in pounds sterling and include everything except delivery, which
    is shown separately before you pay.
  </p>

  <h2>Colour choices</h2>
  <p>
    You choose your colours when you order — on the product page, or during
    checkout where a product has several coloured parts. I print what you
    selected. Please check your selections
    before paying — if you spot a mistake, email me quickly and I will change it
    if printing has not started.
  </p>
  <p>
    Filament colours vary slightly between batches, and screens vary more.
    Photographs are a good guide, not an exact match.
  </p>

  <h2>What you are buying</h2>
  <p>
    These are 3D printed objects made to order. Layer lines are visible, small
    variations between prints are normal, and dimensions may vary by a fraction
    of a millimetre. None of that is a fault.
  </p>

  <h2>Payment</h2>
  <p>
    Payments are handled by Stripe. I never see or store your card details.
  </p>

  <h2>Delivery, cancellation and refunds</h2>
  <p>
    See <a href="/shipping/">Shipping</a> and
    <a href="/returns/">Returns and cancellations</a>. Nothing in these terms
    affects your statutory rights.
  </p>

  <h2>Third-party games and trademarks</h2>
  <p>
    Birdworks is not affiliated with, endorsed by, or connected to any game
    publisher. Where a product is described as working with a particular game,
    that describes compatibility only. All trademarks belong to their owners.
  </p>

  <h2>Liability</h2>
  <p>
    I am responsible for loss you suffer as a foreseeable result of my breaking
    these terms or failing to use reasonable care. I do not limit liability
    where the law does not allow it — including for death or personal injury
    caused by negligence, or for fraud.
  </p>

  <h2>Complaints and law</h2>
  <p>
    Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and I will reply
    within five working days. These terms are governed by the law of England and
    Wales.
  </p>
</Prose>
